  "question": "Would an annotation of the SAME STRUCTURE, placed anywhere on the chromosome, absorb as much of the atlas margin as the real annotation does?",
  "not_graded_because": "The frozen acceptance bar does not name this control. Adding a control after seeing the result it bears on, and letting it select a verdict, is the move the bar exists to prevent. No threshold is read here and no verdict is computed; the published FRAME_PARTIAL and its resolved=false status are untouched. These numbers are for the user to decide on.",
  "why_this_control_replaces_the_proposed_one": "The proposed shuffled-window control was measured invalid first (wiki/promoteratlas_frame_column_split_2026-11-05.json): frame_features takes window information only as the union mask, so relocating windows leaves the two CDS-derived columns byte-identical, and those two columns ALONE match the full five-column table (0.3183 against 0.3170; at least the full table on 6 of 10 seeds). A circular rotation of the whole annotation regenerates BOTH halves, so nothing is invariant.",
